1
00:00:06,006 --> 00:00:08,550
- [Ruru] Okay, let's head back.
- [Ma-kun] Sounds good. See ya.

2
00:00:08,633 --> 00:00:09,509
[Ruru] Bye-bye.

3
00:00:10,385 --> 00:00:12,512
- I'm back!
- Come on in.

4
00:00:12,595 --> 00:00:15,557
- No sauna magic, I'm afraid.
- What?

5
00:00:15,640 --> 00:00:17,642
- [Assun] Why not?
- [Ruru] Well, you know…

6
00:00:17,726 --> 00:00:18,643
RURU (26)
MODEL

7
00:00:18,727 --> 00:00:21,062
I said, "If you wanted to eat <i>yakiniku,</i>

8
00:00:21,146 --> 00:00:24,357
but your girlfriend wanted to eat sushi,
then what would you do?"

9
00:00:24,441 --> 00:00:28,361
And he was like, "Well, if I want
<i>yakiniku,</i> then that's what we're eating."

10
00:00:28,445 --> 00:00:30,572
- He was like, "No compromise."
- Oh, God.

11
00:00:30,655 --> 00:00:32,782
- [Hikaru] I see how it is.
- [Assun] That's a red flag.

12
00:00:32,866 --> 00:00:34,242
[Ruru] That's what I was thinking.

13
00:00:34,325 --> 00:00:37,912
How's he so different when we try
to have deep conversations one-on-one?

14
00:00:37,996 --> 00:00:40,040
You get a totally different impression
one-on-one.

15
00:00:40,123 --> 00:00:42,500
That's wild.
He's more immature than I thought.

16
00:00:42,584 --> 00:00:46,421
Exactly! I don't know, for some reason,
I expected him to be way more mature.

17
00:00:46,504 --> 00:00:48,006
Yeah, honestly, I don't know.

18
00:00:48,089 --> 00:00:49,466
ASSUN (30)
ENTREPRENEUR AND HOSTESS

19
00:00:49,549 --> 00:00:51,926
- [Maririn] Hard pass.
- [Ruru] I'm disappointed.

20
00:00:52,510 --> 00:00:55,263
He's just a pretty face.
That's all he has.

21
00:00:58,767 --> 00:01:01,311
Didn't the letter thing
make your heart pound?

22
00:01:01,394 --> 00:01:03,855
[Tai-chan] It was nerve-wracking.
Whose did you put yours in?

23
00:01:03,938 --> 00:01:05,398
- Whose mailbox?
- [Tai-chan] Mmm.

24
00:01:05,482 --> 00:01:07,567
- Tai-chan thinks she gave him her letter.
- Right.

25
00:01:07,650 --> 00:01:08,735
Interesting.

26
00:01:08,818 --> 00:01:09,861
Honestly…

27
00:01:11,029 --> 00:01:13,531
Mmm… Ma-kun. [giggles]

28
00:01:14,240 --> 00:01:15,825
Wait, then who put one in mine?

29
00:01:16,993 --> 00:01:18,620
Well, you know who now.

30
00:01:19,412 --> 00:01:21,748
So it's her? Maririn.

31
00:01:22,499 --> 00:01:24,542
- Okay, I get it.
- That's it.

32
00:01:25,960 --> 00:01:28,296
I just assumed that
the letter was from you.

33
00:01:28,379 --> 00:01:29,964
Oh, did you really?

34
00:01:31,174 --> 00:01:33,176
Do the girls hate me?
Did I make a bad impression?

35
00:01:33,259 --> 00:01:34,093
- Not at all.
- Really?

36
00:01:34,177 --> 00:01:37,055
Yeah, it's still the first day.
Or, it's been 24 hours.

37
00:01:37,138 --> 00:01:41,309
I mean, still, by now it's pretty clear
I have strong feelings for you, right?

38
00:01:42,268 --> 00:01:43,102
I'd say so.

39
00:01:45,438 --> 00:01:46,898
So you're down to two choices now.

40
00:01:50,610 --> 00:01:52,821
[Tai-chan] I'm quick with everything.
I like to go fast.

41
00:01:52,904 --> 00:01:54,447
- Even saying how I feel.
- [Hikaru] Mmm.

42
00:01:54,531 --> 00:01:56,407
That can be both, good and bad.

43
00:01:57,283 --> 00:01:59,077
I'm a speedster, what can I say?

44
00:01:59,160 --> 00:02:01,746
- You're a speedster? [chuckles]
- [Tai-chan] Big time. No doubt.

45
00:02:06,126 --> 00:02:10,964
Look, I mean, Ruru is a model, so yeah,
part of me was attracted to her.

46
00:02:11,589 --> 00:02:13,716
But right now,
I'm getting close to Hikaru,

47
00:02:13,800 --> 00:02:15,969
or it's more like my feelings for her are…

48
00:02:16,719 --> 00:02:17,846
speeding way up.

49
00:02:19,097 --> 00:02:21,099
[opening theme song playing]

50
00:02:32,026 --> 00:02:34,237
A YANKII DATING REALITY SHOW
WHERE LOVE LIVES ON THE EDGE

51
00:02:35,029 --> 00:02:37,115
RAPPER FROM SAGAMIHARA
SPITTING LYRICS OF PURE LOVE

52
00:02:37,198 --> 00:02:38,783
ARI

53
00:02:38,867 --> 00:02:40,827
KAWASAKI'S IT-GIRL HOSTESS
OUT TO FIND A REAL MAN

54
00:02:40,910 --> 00:02:41,995
HIKARU

55
00:02:42,078 --> 00:02:43,746
KYOTO BAR OWNER
GOING ALL-IN FOR HIS WOMAN

56
00:02:45,039 --> 00:02:46,666
NANIWA'S BARROOM BEAUTY
LOOKING FOR TRUE LOVE

57
00:02:46,749 --> 00:02:47,834
MARIRIN

58
00:02:47,917 --> 00:02:49,294
KURUME YANKII
WHO GREW UP BEHIND BARS

59
00:02:49,377 --> 00:02:50,503
BO

60
00:02:52,714 --> 00:02:54,382
EX-YAKUZA MMA FIGHTER
LOOKING FOR HIS RIDE-OR-DIE

61
00:02:54,465 --> 00:02:55,842
MA-KUN

62
00:02:55,925 --> 00:02:57,719
NAGOYA'S NO.1 HOSTESS
WHO PUTS MEN IN THEIR PLACE

63
00:02:57,802 --> 00:02:58,803
ASSUN

64
00:02:58,887 --> 00:03:00,263
FACE-TATTOOED STYLIST
WHO LOVES HARD

65
00:03:00,346 --> 00:03:01,723
TAI-CHAN

66
00:03:01,806 --> 00:03:03,016
AN HONEST MODEL
IN SEARCH OF LOVE

67
00:03:03,099 --> 00:03:04,183
RURU

68
00:03:08,104 --> 00:03:10,857
BRING ON THE FIGHTS
BRING ON THE LOVE

69
00:03:44,015 --> 00:03:45,099
Right, let's eat!

70
00:03:45,183 --> 00:03:47,185
- [Maririn] Dig in.
- [Tai-chan] Let's eat!

71
00:03:48,937 --> 00:03:49,854
Looks delicious.

72
00:03:49,938 --> 00:03:52,232
- What is this again?
- Carbonara?

73
00:03:52,315 --> 00:03:53,983
- Wait, are you sure?
- Oh, is that wrong?

74
00:03:54,067 --> 00:03:56,361
Why don't we dive deeper
into Maririn's story today?

75
00:03:56,444 --> 00:03:58,321
- [Ruru] Totally.
- [Assun] You want to?

76
00:03:58,404 --> 00:04:00,949
- [Ruru] I want to hear more from her.
- Can I have a drink first?

77
00:04:01,032 --> 00:04:04,327
- [Assun] It's tough to do it sober.
- Don't know if "tough" is the word, but…

78
00:04:04,410 --> 00:04:05,787
Let's give her the floor.

79
00:04:06,412 --> 00:04:08,164
- [Ari] I want to hear.
- [Assun] Go ahead.

80
00:04:08,248 --> 00:04:10,875
[Ma-kun] You should talk too.
Anything to share, Maririn?

81
00:04:10,959 --> 00:04:14,045
But you don't have to force yourself.
It's only been two days.

82
00:04:14,128 --> 00:04:16,589
[Assun] True.
Just whenever you feel like talking.

83
00:04:16,673 --> 00:04:18,549
Probably be easier
if she had booze in her.

84
00:04:18,633 --> 00:04:20,260
[Ma-kun] Wanna wait till we're drinking?

85
00:04:20,843 --> 00:04:23,096
- It's okay, it doesn't have to be today.
- [Assun] Yeah.

86
00:04:26,015 --> 00:04:27,767
- Huh?
- [Nagano] Wait, what's wrong?

87
00:04:27,850 --> 00:04:29,269
What's going on?

88
00:04:30,979 --> 00:04:32,480
- [Bo] What's wrong?
- [sniffles]

89
00:04:32,563 --> 00:04:34,565
- Some stuff is coming up.
- [Leo] Hey, it's okay.

90
00:04:37,610 --> 00:04:38,736
MA-KUN (28)
MMA FIGHTER

91
00:04:38,820 --> 00:04:40,363
You okay, Maririn? What's up?

92
00:04:40,446 --> 00:04:43,700
- [Maririn sobbing]
- [Ruru] You don't have to talk about it.

93
00:04:43,783 --> 00:04:45,868
- [Leo] Don't push yourself.
- [Ruru] Exactly.

94
00:04:45,952 --> 00:04:48,997
Yeah. Oh, hey, you shouldn't open
a letter with "Wassup."

95
00:04:49,080 --> 00:04:50,206
ARI (29)
RAPPER & MODEL

96
00:04:50,290 --> 00:04:52,500
- [Leo] Seriously.
- [Ma-kun] That's crazy, man. No way.

97
00:04:52,583 --> 00:04:54,877
[Assun] We laughed so hard
when we saw that.

98
00:04:54,961 --> 00:04:56,421
- [Ari] Who'd do that?
- He did.

99
00:04:56,504 --> 00:04:57,880
- [Ari] Come on.
- Go smoke?

100
00:04:57,964 --> 00:04:59,924
- I wanna go with you, Hikaru.
- [Hikaru] Wanna go?

101
00:05:00,425 --> 00:05:02,552
- [Ruru] Huh?
- Should we go?

102
00:05:04,304 --> 00:05:06,431
You want to? [sniffles]

103
00:05:10,268 --> 00:05:13,062
BRING ON LIFE

104
00:05:13,646 --> 00:05:16,024
Classrooms?
Whoa, this is crazy. [chuckles]

105
00:05:16,107 --> 00:05:17,650
[Tai-chan] Takes you back, doesn't it?

106
00:05:19,944 --> 00:05:20,820
[Maririn chuckles]

107
00:05:20,903 --> 00:05:22,613
Let's gaze into
each other's eyes and talk.

108
00:05:22,697 --> 00:05:24,073
- Gaze into your eyes?
- Yeah.

109
00:05:24,157 --> 00:05:26,117
- [sighs]
- [Tai-chan] Why were you crying earlier?

110
00:05:28,369 --> 00:05:31,205
- Don't have to say if you don't want to.
- Mmm. [sniffles]

111
00:05:34,417 --> 00:05:38,171
Well, uh, honestly, like,
I don't even know where to start.

112
00:05:38,254 --> 00:05:39,380
- [Tai-chan] Yeah.
- [sniffles]

113
00:05:40,214 --> 00:05:44,719
But, like, all my boyfriends were abusive,
and the worst guy I was with was…

114
00:05:45,678 --> 00:05:48,765
He was basically a thug.
Like, just a bad guy in general.

115
00:05:48,848 --> 00:05:51,684
This one time
he grabbed my head and… [sniffles]

116
00:05:51,768 --> 00:05:54,645
…he kept saying he was going to,
like, cut me open,

117
00:05:54,729 --> 00:05:58,024
and make me bleed out
and rip off my nails in the bathroom.

118
00:05:58,107 --> 00:06:00,902
[sniffles] And he was serious,
told me to go in there.

119
00:06:01,652 --> 00:06:03,821
I know he'd actually killed someone too,

120
00:06:03,905 --> 00:06:07,241
and he pointed a gun at me
and stuff, so… [exhales]

121
00:06:07,867 --> 00:06:10,328
I don't know,
he basically took everything I had.

122
00:06:10,411 --> 00:06:11,788
He destroyed my whole life.

123
00:06:12,371 --> 00:06:13,331
Huh?

124
00:06:14,290 --> 00:06:15,458
[sniffles] So, yeah.

125
00:06:16,918 --> 00:06:18,336
I just… [sobs]

126
00:06:20,004 --> 00:06:22,340
I've never been loved by anyone, and…

127
00:06:24,175 --> 00:06:27,345
[sobbing, sniffling]

128
00:06:29,180 --> 00:06:32,350
And I don't know why
I've had to go through this much pain.

129
00:06:33,309 --> 00:06:36,771
I don't even know who he was,
he lied about his name and everything.

130
00:06:38,272 --> 00:06:39,190
So, yeah.

131
00:06:40,775 --> 00:06:42,902
I mean,
that's a pretty heavy story, right?

132
00:06:44,403 --> 00:06:45,404
I feel like…

133
00:06:46,739 --> 00:06:50,451
that heaviness is coming out here
and I seem really gloomy to everyone.

134
00:06:50,535 --> 00:06:52,328
I don't know how to have
a real relationship.

135
00:06:52,411 --> 00:06:54,831
A lot of times I go along
with whatever the other person says

136
00:06:54,914 --> 00:06:56,749
'cause I'm afraid I'm gonna get hit.

137
00:06:56,833 --> 00:06:59,919
So, I always end up kind of
fading into the background.

138
00:07:00,461 --> 00:07:02,964
And it gets harder and harder
to express myself.

139
00:07:05,299 --> 00:07:06,300
[sniffles]

140
00:07:08,719 --> 00:07:10,471
- Sorry.
- Dang, that's… Yeah.

141
00:07:10,555 --> 00:07:12,515
[Maririn chuckles, sniffles] Yeah.

142
00:07:13,641 --> 00:07:16,144
Sorry. Thanks. [laughs, sniffles]

143
00:07:16,227 --> 00:07:18,813
You can't just share that, I get it.
Not in a group.

144
00:07:19,981 --> 00:07:21,357
But the thing is, like…

145
00:07:22,817 --> 00:07:25,278
I do really want to be loved by someone

146
00:07:26,529 --> 00:07:28,781
'cause I don't know
what real love is like.

147
00:07:30,825 --> 00:07:33,411
I thought if I came here…

148
00:07:35,830 --> 00:07:38,416
someone might finally
express real feelings for me.

149
00:07:40,084 --> 00:07:42,503
Thanks for listening
while looking me in the eye.

150
00:07:42,587 --> 00:07:43,671
No problem.

151
00:07:45,047 --> 00:07:46,340
And, yeah, I…

152
00:07:46,424 --> 00:07:48,050
I guess I do feel better getting it out

153
00:07:48,134 --> 00:07:49,927
'cause I don't really
tell people about this.

154
00:07:50,011 --> 00:07:51,095
[Tai-chan] Oh, right.

155
00:07:51,679 --> 00:07:53,681
- [Maririn] This isn't too heavy?
- No way.

156
00:07:53,764 --> 00:07:55,308
- [Maririn] You really mean that?
- Yeah.

157
00:07:55,933 --> 00:07:58,019
[Maririn] Anyway, um, thanks. [sniffles]

158
00:07:58,936 --> 00:08:01,522
I hope that we can both experience…

159
00:08:01,606 --> 00:08:03,399
- [Maririn] Mmm.
- …real love here.

160
00:08:03,483 --> 00:08:05,109
[Nagano] <i>Tai-chan's a good guy.</i>

161
00:08:05,193 --> 00:08:06,819
I'm glad you invited me.

162
00:08:06,903 --> 00:08:08,613
- [Tai-chan] Yeah?
- Thanks for inviting me.

163
00:08:08,696 --> 00:08:10,531
- [Tai-chan] Don't mention it.
- [chuckles]

164
00:08:10,615 --> 00:08:12,450
[Megumi] <i>It turns out that Maririn</i>

165
00:08:12,533 --> 00:08:14,160
<i>- has some serious scars.</i>
- [Nagano] <i>Right?</i>

166
00:08:15,286 --> 00:08:17,788
- [Ari] Let's take a picture.
- [Hikaru] A Polaroid! Let's do it!

167
00:08:18,998 --> 00:08:21,042
- On three, "Wassup, man,"
- [both] One, two, three.

168
00:08:21,125 --> 00:08:23,252
- Wassup, man!
- [giggles]

169
00:08:23,336 --> 00:08:24,504
Amazing. [laughs]

170
00:08:24,587 --> 00:08:26,255
- Not bad at all.
- What was that?

171
00:08:26,339 --> 00:08:28,216
We nailed this one.
I think it's the first time

172
00:08:28,299 --> 00:08:30,051
- I've taken a Polaroid with a girl.
- Me too.

173
00:08:30,134 --> 00:08:31,135
- Really?
- Mmm-hmm.

174
00:08:31,219 --> 00:08:33,638
I feel like the two of us,
out of everyone here,

175
00:08:33,721 --> 00:08:35,973
people see us as the jokers,
the loudmouths,

176
00:08:36,057 --> 00:08:39,185
but it's interesting to see what it's like
when it's just the two of us.

177
00:08:39,268 --> 00:08:42,522
- Mmm. They see us like the class clowns.
- Very much so. [laughs]

178
00:08:42,605 --> 00:08:45,316
- Like, we don't know what's going on?
- Totally.

179
00:08:45,399 --> 00:08:48,361
No, exactly.
But I think we're serious when it matters.

180
00:08:48,444 --> 00:08:50,112
- Like when it comes to love.
- Mmm.

181
00:08:50,196 --> 00:08:51,906
I'm definitely misunderstood.

182
00:08:51,989 --> 00:08:55,826
Especially 'cause I work at a hostess bar,
so people assume I'm a total slut.

183
00:08:55,910 --> 00:08:57,119
But I'm really innocent.

184
00:08:57,912 --> 00:08:59,747
Hey, boss,
are we allowed to say "slut" here?

185
00:08:59,830 --> 00:09:02,500
- [chuckles]
- We've decided to let it slide this once.

186
00:09:02,583 --> 00:09:03,960
Oh, very nice.

187
00:09:04,710 --> 00:09:05,878
- You're from Kanagawa?
- Mmm.

188
00:09:05,962 --> 00:09:07,713
Me too.
Kawasaki is close to where you are?

189
00:09:07,797 --> 00:09:08,798
- Yeah.
- We're close enough

190
00:09:08,881 --> 00:09:11,634
- that rumors about me could reach you.
- [Ari] I gotcha.

191
00:09:11,717 --> 00:09:13,511
But, whatever you hear about me,

192
00:09:13,594 --> 00:09:16,138
there's no way it'll be that I'm a slut.
No chance.

193
00:09:16,222 --> 00:09:18,182
- [Ari] 'Cause you're the opposite?
- Yup.

194
00:09:18,266 --> 00:09:21,519
Oh, okay, gotcha.
Damn, that hit me kinda hard just now.

195
00:09:21,602 --> 00:09:23,854
You saying,
"You'll never hear that about me".

196
00:09:23,938 --> 00:09:25,398
I've never heard that before.

197
00:09:25,481 --> 00:09:27,567
- That's really rare.
- I'm legit innocent.

198
00:09:27,650 --> 00:09:29,360
Good to know.

199
00:09:29,443 --> 00:09:32,446
Wait, so is there someone
you're interested in right now?

200
00:09:32,530 --> 00:09:34,198
Like, are you vibing with anyone?

201
00:09:34,782 --> 00:09:37,410
Honestly, I hope not.
I hope it's just me, you know?

202
00:09:38,244 --> 00:09:40,746
- Why are you smirking? [chuckles]
- [Hikaru giggles]

203
00:09:44,250 --> 00:09:46,752
You have my letter
in your pocket, don't you?

204
00:09:46,836 --> 00:09:48,921
- Yeah. Why do you ask?
- Why? Because I actually--

205
00:09:49,005 --> 00:09:52,675
I have super sloppy handwriting,
and I half-assed it because I was wasted.

206
00:09:53,384 --> 00:09:55,928
- Thanks for this.
- [laughing] No, stop it.

207
00:09:56,971 --> 00:10:00,433
- [Tai-chan] Want me to stop?
- No, you can keep looking at it. [laughs]

208
00:10:01,142 --> 00:10:02,059
Um… [sniffles]

209
00:10:02,685 --> 00:10:05,146
No, I wanna write it again,
but better this time.

210
00:10:06,147 --> 00:10:07,773
- [chuckles]
- [Nagano exclaims]

211
00:10:07,857 --> 00:10:10,276
- [Megumi] <i>She's here.</i>
- Excuse me. Sorry, guys.

212
00:10:11,569 --> 00:10:13,988
- Can I crash your party for a second?
- [Maririn] Crash away.

213
00:10:14,071 --> 00:10:15,406
- [Tai-chan] Sure.
- [Maririn] Yeah.

214
00:10:15,489 --> 00:10:18,242
- There goes the "Let you have him."
- "Can I crash your party?"

215
00:10:18,326 --> 00:10:21,120
<i>- She's something, isn't she?</i>
- [Megumi] <i>How can she just</i>

216
00:10:21,203 --> 00:10:23,623
<i>- barge into a conversation like that?</i>
- [Nagano] <i>I don't know.</i>

217
00:10:23,706 --> 00:10:24,707
What should I do?

218
00:10:25,499 --> 00:10:27,835
Are the three of us
going to talk together? Or…

219
00:10:28,753 --> 00:10:30,796
- Either way is…
- Okay if we chat alone for a second?

220
00:10:30,880 --> 00:10:32,340
- [Maririn] For sure.
- [Hikaru] Cool?

221
00:10:32,423 --> 00:10:33,591
[Maririn] You gonna go smoke?

222
00:10:33,674 --> 00:10:35,134
- Do you mind?
- Go ahead.

223
00:10:35,217 --> 00:10:38,554
- Right, then. Sorry, okay?
- [Maririn] No worries. [chuckles softly]

224
00:10:41,766 --> 00:10:42,767
[Tai-chan] Okay…

225
00:10:43,768 --> 00:10:45,811
I mean…

226
00:10:45,895 --> 00:10:48,522
- The girls are assertive.
- Finally, moves are being made!

227
00:10:48,606 --> 00:10:50,900
- Definitely some palpable tension there.
- Here we go!

228
00:10:51,901 --> 00:10:54,195
- Real quick. Hmm?
- [Tai-chan] So you came back to me, huh?

229
00:10:54,278 --> 00:10:55,696
- I thought you would.
- [Hikaru] Why?

230
00:10:55,780 --> 00:10:56,864
[Tai-chan] You came back.

231
00:10:57,657 --> 00:11:00,284
- What do you mean by, "You came back"?
- Glad you did.

232
00:11:00,368 --> 00:11:02,078
But, then again, you're the guy.

233
00:11:02,161 --> 00:11:03,579
- Mmm.
- Know what I mean?

234
00:11:03,663 --> 00:11:05,081
- Huh?
- You're the guy.

235
00:11:05,164 --> 00:11:07,249
- What do you mean?
- You're the guy, right?

236
00:11:07,333 --> 00:11:08,626
- I am a guy.
- I mean…

237
00:11:08,709 --> 00:11:10,503
[Tai-chan] I should've come to get you?

238
00:11:10,586 --> 00:11:12,672
- [Hikaru scoffs] Obviously.
- [Tai-chan] Right, sorry.

239
00:11:13,255 --> 00:11:16,050
- It's not like that. Hear me out.
- Remember what you said earlier?

240
00:11:16,133 --> 00:11:17,301
[Tai-chan] Hmm? Yeah.

241
00:11:18,052 --> 00:11:19,095
- Earlier?
- Hmm.

242
00:11:19,178 --> 00:11:21,639
- That you were torn between two people.
- Oh, yeah.

243
00:11:21,722 --> 00:11:24,517
- I feel like you're not torn, though.
- No, listen.

244
00:11:24,600 --> 00:11:28,437
Earlier, when we were all talking,
she was crying, right?

245
00:11:28,521 --> 00:11:30,106
- It took me off guard.
- Mmm-hmm.

246
00:11:30,606 --> 00:11:32,566
Not about that. That's not what I mean.

247
00:11:32,650 --> 00:11:34,860
The reason why I came
to get you just now is,

248
00:11:34,944 --> 00:11:36,362
earlier today, you kind of…

249
00:11:36,445 --> 00:11:38,948
made it seem like you were torn
between two people,

250
00:11:39,031 --> 00:11:40,699
so I was like, "Wait, what the…"

251
00:11:41,450 --> 00:11:42,451
Mmm.

252
00:11:43,077 --> 00:11:44,703
- When the timing…
- [Hikaru] Mmm.

253
00:11:44,787 --> 00:11:47,498
…was right for me to leave,
I was gonna go see…

254
00:11:48,874 --> 00:11:50,709
- I told you that, didn't I?
- Mmm-hmm.

255
00:11:50,793 --> 00:11:53,003
So, yeah, the plan was to come to you.

256
00:11:53,087 --> 00:11:54,380
- Really?
- [Tai-chan] Yeah.

257
00:11:55,089 --> 00:11:56,924
- I wanted to.
- Okay, yeah.

258
00:11:57,007 --> 00:11:59,176
- Sorry about that.
- I kinda want you to be forward.

259
00:11:59,260 --> 00:12:02,263
- Oh, really?
- Yeah, if that's how you really feel.

260
00:12:02,346 --> 00:12:04,390
If you mean it
when you say you're interested in me,

261
00:12:04,473 --> 00:12:05,808
you can be more assertive.

262
00:12:06,684 --> 00:12:09,103
The fact that I'm the youngest,
for some reason,

263
00:12:09,186 --> 00:12:12,523
- is really holding me back inside--
- Age is nothing but a number.

264
00:12:12,606 --> 00:12:16,277
- Agree. Age gaps don't mean anything.
- [Hikaru] It doesn't matter, at all.

265
00:12:16,360 --> 00:12:18,154
Yeah, I can be more forward.

266
00:12:18,237 --> 00:12:19,738
I mean, sometimes age matters,

267
00:12:19,822 --> 00:12:21,657
- but out in society.
- I wanna talk one-on-one.

268
00:12:21,740 --> 00:12:23,492
Let's do it. Cool. Invite me.

269
00:12:23,576 --> 00:12:26,328
For sure, I will.
'Cause I think you're super cute.

270
00:12:26,412 --> 00:12:27,830
- That makes me happy.
- Yeah?

271
00:12:29,165 --> 00:12:31,584
- Keep telling me I'm cute, okay?
- [Tai-chan] I can do that.

272
00:12:31,667 --> 00:12:33,669
I'll make sure
I start first thing in the morning.

273
00:12:33,752 --> 00:12:36,297
- Sneak over to your bed.
- [chuckles]

274
00:12:38,716 --> 00:12:41,844
- [Tai-chan]<i> I'll say it all the time.</i>
- [Hikaru]<i> But act like you mean it too.</i>

275
00:12:41,927 --> 00:12:44,597
[Tai-chan]<i> If I didn't plan to,</i>
<i>it wouldn't make sense to be here.</i>

276
00:12:44,680 --> 00:12:45,598
[Hikaru]<i> That's right.</i>

277
00:12:45,681 --> 00:12:48,142
[Tai-chan]<i> And if I do something</i>
<i>out of pocket, just smack me.</i>

278
00:12:48,225 --> 00:12:49,852
- <i>Don't hold back.</i>
- [Hikaru]<i> Okay.</i>

279
00:12:49,935 --> 00:12:52,021
[Tai-chan]
<i>Slap me and say, "You're all talk!"</i>

280
00:12:52,104 --> 00:12:54,607
- Maririn!
- She's writing another letter all alone?

281
00:12:54,690 --> 00:12:57,401
- Heartbreaking. [groans]
- [Megumi exclaims]

282
00:12:58,694 --> 00:13:00,362
I wanna get to know you better.

283
00:13:00,446 --> 00:13:02,865
I want us both
to get to know each other, so…

284
00:13:02,948 --> 00:13:04,575
- [Tai-chan] Wanna be real with me?
- Yeah.

285
00:13:04,658 --> 00:13:06,076
[Tai-chan] I want that too. A lot.

286
00:13:06,160 --> 00:13:08,370
- I can't stand fake people.
- Can I interrupt?

287
00:13:08,454 --> 00:13:09,288
- Yeah.
- For sure.

288
00:13:09,371 --> 00:13:11,499
- I actually rewrote my letter.
- Oh.

289
00:13:11,582 --> 00:13:14,043
- You can read it in your room later.
- [Tai-chan] Will do.

290
00:13:16,545 --> 00:13:17,963
- Thanks.
- Thanks. Sorry about that.

291
00:13:19,632 --> 00:13:21,634
What does she mean, rewrote her letter?

292
00:13:22,593 --> 00:13:24,553
- [Tai-chan] Hey, keep it down.
- What did she mean?

293
00:13:24,637 --> 00:13:26,430
- [Tai-chan] The letter from yesterday?
- Yeah.

294
00:13:26,514 --> 00:13:28,307
[Tai-chan]
It was based on first impressions…

295
00:13:32,853 --> 00:13:34,855
[mellow music playing]

296
00:13:44,198 --> 00:13:47,743
[Maririn] <i>Well, basically,</i>
<i>I wrote that I was interested in him. And</i>…

297
00:13:47,826 --> 00:13:50,788
<i>Also, like, um,</i>
<i>when he left the room with Hikaru,</i>

298
00:13:50,871 --> 00:13:53,207
<i>he said something like, "I'm sorry, okay?"</i>

299
00:13:53,290 --> 00:13:56,877
So I put in the letter that
I got a little jealous in that moment.

300
00:13:57,586 --> 00:14:00,631
I just hope it gives him
a sense of how I feel. That's all.

301
00:14:00,714 --> 00:14:02,716
He's been carrying my letter around.

302
00:14:03,300 --> 00:14:05,511
I just thought that was really cute.

303
00:14:05,594 --> 00:14:09,515
I didn't think she'd go out of her way
like that to rewrite the letter.

304
00:14:11,058 --> 00:14:12,393
But the thing is,

305
00:14:12,977 --> 00:14:17,523
I can't help that Hikaru is kind of
always on my mind, so it's kind of… Yeah.

306
00:14:20,693 --> 00:14:22,069
So, how was the sauna?

307
00:14:22,152 --> 00:14:26,448
Well, I think for me, it made me realize
I might be more interested in you, Leo.

308
00:14:26,532 --> 00:14:28,242
More than Mao… or, Ma-kun.

309
00:14:28,325 --> 00:14:30,327
- What?
- [Megumi] Oh, my, my, my, my.

310
00:14:31,078 --> 00:14:32,997
- After going to the sauna today?
- Yeah.

311
00:14:33,080 --> 00:14:34,665
- Why's that?
- I didn't really…

312
00:14:34,748 --> 00:14:37,167
feel the sauna magic
with Ma-kun, you know?

313
00:14:37,251 --> 00:14:38,294
Oh…

314
00:14:40,671 --> 00:14:42,381
Like, I kept genuinely thinking,

315
00:14:42,464 --> 00:14:45,676
"Oh, I'd rather be talking
to Leo right now instead of Ma-kun."

316
00:14:45,759 --> 00:14:48,512
Mmm. That makes me happy too.

317
00:14:49,680 --> 00:14:52,182
I was really moved by your letter.
I mean it.

318
00:14:52,266 --> 00:14:53,392
[Ruru] Oh, seriously?

319
00:14:53,475 --> 00:14:54,476
For real.

320
00:14:55,561 --> 00:14:56,854
- It hit me hard.
- Mmm.

321
00:14:56,937 --> 00:14:58,188
Like, I'm already, uh…

322
00:14:59,815 --> 00:15:02,568
When I first showed up here,
with everyone,

323
00:15:02,651 --> 00:15:04,612
- I was in full-on bad boy mode.
- Mmm.

324
00:15:04,695 --> 00:15:06,864
That's fading
and love is taking its place.

325
00:15:08,449 --> 00:15:09,450
Wow.

326
00:15:09,950 --> 00:15:11,785
- Super happy to hear that.
- [Leo] I mean that.

327
00:15:11,869 --> 00:15:14,121
Your letter took my breath away,
I told everyone that.

328
00:15:14,204 --> 00:15:15,331
- That's so cool.
- [Leo] Yeah.

329
00:15:16,081 --> 00:15:18,584
But the moment you went to the sauna,
I was back in fight mode.

330
00:15:18,667 --> 00:15:20,836
[laughs]

331
00:15:21,795 --> 00:15:23,380
With Leo, I kind of…

332
00:15:24,048 --> 00:15:26,884
I didn't get butterflies,
and I don't really know why.

333
00:15:27,509 --> 00:15:29,219
[exclaiming]

334
00:15:30,387 --> 00:15:33,307
- What is wrong with her?
- Yeah, I wonder what her deal is.

335
00:15:33,390 --> 00:15:35,684
I just didn't feel a romantic spark.

336
00:15:36,393 --> 00:15:37,311
So, yeah.

337
00:15:38,187 --> 00:15:40,064
It's kind of a mystery, even to me.

338
00:15:40,606 --> 00:15:43,943
I couldn't tell you why
there wasn't a stronger connection there.

339
00:15:44,026 --> 00:15:45,903
But I wanna keep getting to know him.

340
00:15:45,986 --> 00:15:49,198
I kind of want him to do something
about his fashion choices.

341
00:15:49,949 --> 00:15:52,409
Come on, Leo's outfit today was so lame.

342
00:15:52,493 --> 00:15:54,620
His style just makes him
look like a party animal,

343
00:15:54,703 --> 00:15:57,748
<i>those tight-fitting jeans</i>
<i>that have a cheap looking-wash.</i>

344
00:15:57,831 --> 00:15:59,124
<i>The whole time, I was thinking,</i>

345
00:15:59,208 --> 00:16:03,629
<i>"No bad boy would be caught dead</i>
<i>in those pants in the 21st century."</i>

346
00:16:03,712 --> 00:16:08,175
In the end, it's about personality,
but fashion sense is really important too.

347
00:16:08,258 --> 00:16:09,510
For both, men and women.

348
00:16:09,593 --> 00:16:11,261
[bell chiming]

349
00:16:11,345 --> 00:16:12,638
- [Ari] Morning.
- [Leo] Hey, guys.

350
00:16:12,721 --> 00:16:14,640
- [Maririn] Morning.
- [Ma-kun] Morning.

351
00:16:14,723 --> 00:16:16,850
- [Leo] Here we go.
<i>- </i>[boy on PA] <i>Time for Ethics class.</i>

352
00:16:16,934 --> 00:16:18,894
<i>Life begins when you stop running</i>

353
00:16:18,978 --> 00:16:21,647
<i>from your past, and embrace who you are.</i>

354
00:16:22,398 --> 00:16:25,359
<i>Please reflect on the mistakes</i>
<i>you've made in your life,</i>

355
00:16:25,442 --> 00:16:27,778
<i>and discuss them amongst yourselves.</i>

356
00:16:28,570 --> 00:16:31,615
<i>Listen with compassion</i>
<i>to the regrets of others,</i>

357
00:16:31,699 --> 00:16:34,910
<i>and try to learn from them.</i>
<i>Think about your own mistakes.</i>

358
00:16:34,994 --> 00:16:37,454
[Ari] They do this discussion thing
in other countries, right?

359
00:16:37,538 --> 00:16:38,956
[boy on PA] <i>First up is Bo.</i>

360
00:16:39,039 --> 00:16:40,624
- [Ari] You're up.
<i>- </i>[Boy on PA] <i>Go ahead.</i>

361
00:16:40,708 --> 00:16:43,127
- [Ari] Get up there, Bo.
- [Ruru chuckling]

362
00:16:43,210 --> 00:16:44,378
- Take it away.
- [Ari] Wassup?

363
00:16:44,461 --> 00:16:46,672
- Thank you.
- [Ruru] He's the teacher.

364
00:16:46,755 --> 00:16:47,756
[Bo] Um, let's see…

365
00:16:48,799 --> 00:16:50,884
After I graduated from elementary school,

366
00:16:50,968 --> 00:16:53,804
most of the people around me
were doing really bad stuff.

367
00:16:53,887 --> 00:16:56,598
So I just naturally
fell in with them. [sniffles]

368
00:16:57,266 --> 00:16:58,767
I was about 17 when I got back

369
00:16:58,851 --> 00:17:00,686
from juvenile training school
the second time.

370
00:17:00,769 --> 00:17:04,106
So, after I came back that time,
things were smooth for a while,

371
00:17:04,815 --> 00:17:07,443
and then, when I was 21 or so,

372
00:17:08,318 --> 00:17:11,905
I tried drugs for the first time.
And I struggled a lot.

373
00:17:13,198 --> 00:17:14,867
Who introduced you to meth?

374
00:17:14,950 --> 00:17:18,078
[inhales] It was pretty much friends
and older classmates.

375
00:17:19,455 --> 00:17:21,248
Good job staying clean.

376
00:17:21,331 --> 00:17:23,083
Well, now… Now, it's not that.

377
00:17:23,167 --> 00:17:26,253
Like, after I got out,
I thought about using constantly.

378
00:17:29,214 --> 00:17:31,300
But with the support and love
of people around me,

379
00:17:31,383 --> 00:17:32,801
I was able to move forward in life.

380
00:17:32,885 --> 00:17:34,720
It helps a lot to be here too.

381
00:17:35,679 --> 00:17:39,183
The environment you're in matters,
that's definitely another thing I…

382
00:17:40,100 --> 00:17:41,101
realized.

383
00:17:42,061 --> 00:17:43,854
- Were you shooting up?
- [laughing]

384
00:17:43,937 --> 00:17:45,481
- Or were you smoking?
- Bo.

385
00:17:45,564 --> 00:17:47,357
- You smoked? Which one?
- They're curious.

386
00:17:47,441 --> 00:17:49,526
- I smoked it.
- [Assun] You weren't injecting it.

387
00:17:49,610 --> 00:17:51,570
If I injected,
I probably wouldn't have recovered.

388
00:17:51,653 --> 00:17:52,780
[Maririn] That's true.

389
00:17:52,863 --> 00:17:54,156
There's a difference.

390
00:17:54,239 --> 00:17:55,574
- Just came out and asked?
- Yeah.

391
00:17:55,657 --> 00:17:57,242
You'd be fine if you smoked it.

392
00:17:57,326 --> 00:17:59,536
- [Nagano] Oh, is that so?
- Yeah, just don't inject.

393
00:17:59,620 --> 00:18:02,831
- Some of the stuff Awich says is shocking.
- Yeah, she makes me a little nervous.

394
00:18:02,915 --> 00:18:04,792
There's a big difference.

395
00:18:04,875 --> 00:18:07,628
- You know a lot about this. "Needle?"
- Mmm, that's true.

396
00:18:07,711 --> 00:18:09,922
- Suspicious.
- I'd get it if it was us, but the ladies?

397
00:18:10,005 --> 00:18:12,674
- [Ari] Yeah, the girls.
- [Ma-kun] "Smoking, shooting up"? Chill.

398
00:18:12,758 --> 00:18:14,426
- [Leo laughs]
- But you can't get arrested.

399
00:18:14,510 --> 00:18:15,761
- [Leo] Yeah.
- [Bo] I know.

400
00:18:15,844 --> 00:18:17,763
For all of our sake's, actually.

401
00:18:17,846 --> 00:18:19,223
- [Ruru] Yeah.
- You're right.

402
00:18:19,848 --> 00:18:22,559
- Like, we eat all of our meals together…
- [Ma-kun] Mmm.

403
00:18:22,643 --> 00:18:25,854
- Don't know if I'd say we're family yet--
- We are family. What's wrong with you?

404
00:18:25,938 --> 00:18:27,272
[all laughing]

405
00:18:27,356 --> 00:18:29,525
- [Ruru] What a man.
- Thanks for saying that.

406
00:18:29,608 --> 00:18:33,487
I think all of us probably want you
to take care of yourself

407
00:18:33,570 --> 00:18:35,197
and find happiness in your life.

408
00:18:35,280 --> 00:18:36,448
- [Bo] Hmm.
- Mmm-hmm.

409
00:18:36,532 --> 00:18:38,408
Thanks, guys. [chuckles]

410
00:18:40,744 --> 00:18:44,289
[boy on PA] <i>Thank you.</i>
<i>Maririn, it's your turn. Please stand up.</i>

411
00:18:44,373 --> 00:18:45,374
Okay.

412
00:18:47,126 --> 00:18:48,961
- [laughing]
- [Assun] Ms. Maririn.

413
00:18:49,044 --> 00:18:50,879
- [Ari] Say good morning.
- [Ruru] Take it away.

414
00:18:50,963 --> 00:18:53,715
So the reason my life
went off the rails was…

415
00:18:53,799 --> 00:18:55,008
Well, let's see…

416
00:18:55,592 --> 00:18:58,679
The biggest reason was that
I didn't live with my parents.

417
00:18:59,179 --> 00:19:02,724
I was always a grandma's girl, I guess.
My grandma raised me, so…

418
00:19:02,808 --> 00:19:05,602
The thing is,
I never wanted to be a burden to her.

419
00:19:05,686 --> 00:19:08,897
So, during my first year of middle school,
I started working at night.

420
00:19:08,981 --> 00:19:11,775
Mostly at girls bars.
I kind of hardly went to school.

421
00:19:11,859 --> 00:19:13,318
And I lived in a rented room.

422
00:19:14,236 --> 00:19:15,863
And then… [sighs]

423
00:19:15,946 --> 00:19:18,782
Oh, another reason
why I didn't want to be at home was…

424
00:19:18,866 --> 00:19:21,034
Well, my grandpa would, um, take his cane,

425
00:19:21,118 --> 00:19:26,248
and be like, "Go back to your country."
I'd never even lived there before.

426
00:19:26,331 --> 00:19:28,625
He'd say that over and over
and hit me with his cane.

427
00:19:28,709 --> 00:19:30,377
What?

428
00:19:31,837 --> 00:19:34,548
So, yeah, because of stuff like that,
I didn't want to be at home,

429
00:19:34,631 --> 00:19:37,092
and I did things
I can't tell people about.

430
00:19:37,676 --> 00:19:39,219
- That's about it.
- [Ruru] Mmm.

431
00:19:39,303 --> 00:19:41,471
- [Maririn] I guess that's how it started.
- [Ruru] Mmm.

432
00:19:42,222 --> 00:19:45,142
So basically, your own family
was really racist toward you?

433
00:19:45,225 --> 00:19:48,478
Yeah. My grandpa was from an older
generation, so I kind of get it. Still…

434
00:19:49,688 --> 00:19:51,899
That was tough
for a girl in middle school.

435
00:19:51,982 --> 00:19:54,902
- [Ruru] I bet.
- [Nagano] <i>Oh, my God, what a story.</i>

436
00:19:54,985 --> 00:19:56,862
- [Ari] I can relate to that.
- [Maririn] Mmm.

437
00:19:56,945 --> 00:19:59,489
Even though I'm from Kanagawa,
people would say to me, like,

438
00:19:59,573 --> 00:20:01,116
"Get out of my country" and stuff.

439
00:20:01,200 --> 00:20:04,494
- I was always thinking, "I was born here."
- [Maririn] That's right. Right.

440
00:20:04,578 --> 00:20:07,789
[Ruru] Did your grandma protect you
when your grandpa said that stuff?

441
00:20:07,873 --> 00:20:10,042
She did try to protect me at first, but,

442
00:20:10,125 --> 00:20:13,837
then grandpa started
using his cane on her, and that was that.

443
00:20:13,921 --> 00:20:15,547
- [Assun] Oh…
- So I was like,

444
00:20:15,631 --> 00:20:17,841
"I can't do this.
I'm gonna live on my own."

445
00:20:17,925 --> 00:20:20,344
- [Assun] Mmm.
- [Maririn] It was hard.

446
00:20:22,221 --> 00:20:25,974
Around that time I started thinking,
"Is anyone ever gonna love me?"

447
00:20:26,058 --> 00:20:27,976
All of my boyfriends were abusive.

448
00:20:28,060 --> 00:20:30,604
- [Assun] What?
- [Maririn] That's how it was.

449
00:20:31,188 --> 00:20:33,190
Yeah, so I'm always carrying

450
00:20:33,273 --> 00:20:35,901
- this need to be loved.
- [Assun] Makes sense you'd want affection.

451
00:20:35,984 --> 00:20:39,112
I'm craving it 'cause I don't know
what real love is, or…

452
00:20:39,196 --> 00:20:41,490
My family never showed it to me.

453
00:20:41,573 --> 00:20:45,285
The way families in TV shows hold hands,
hug, play with each other's hair,

454
00:20:45,994 --> 00:20:47,955
I didn't think any of that was real.

455
00:20:48,038 --> 00:20:51,375
That was when I started to think,
"Oh, I'm not normal."

456
00:20:51,458 --> 00:20:54,336
[Assun] But maybe coming here
is an opportunity to change.

457
00:20:54,419 --> 00:20:56,171
Yeah, totally, I think it could be.

458
00:20:56,255 --> 00:20:59,383
You don't get a chance to talk about
your problems like this in the real world.

459
00:20:59,466 --> 00:21:00,467
Mmm.

460
00:21:01,176 --> 00:21:03,470
That's right, and it doesn't
have to be romantic love.

461
00:21:03,553 --> 00:21:06,306
I just want you to experience
genuine connection here.

462
00:21:06,390 --> 00:21:10,060
- Even just the bond between friends.
- The love of a friend can change you.

463
00:21:10,686 --> 00:21:14,022
Just hearing your story really makes me
want to show you that.

464
00:21:14,106 --> 00:21:16,066
- [Assun] Yeah.
- Thanks, guys.

465
00:21:16,149 --> 00:21:18,277
[mellow music playing]

466
00:21:20,028 --> 00:21:22,030
Yeah, I do think friends are important.

467
00:21:22,114 --> 00:21:23,532
- Really important.
- They are.

468
00:21:24,825 --> 00:21:26,743
Right, just someone you can rely on.

469
00:21:27,494 --> 00:21:31,748
I get how hard it is to be in a place
where you don't have that. [sniffles]

470
00:21:31,832 --> 00:21:34,334
And I know not having
any love in your life

471
00:21:34,418 --> 00:21:36,920
probably seems like the norm for you,

472
00:21:37,004 --> 00:21:39,631
but a lot of us here, most of us,
hopefully, we know…

473
00:21:39,715 --> 00:21:40,799
[Maririn] Mmm-hmm.

474
00:21:40,882 --> 00:21:44,594
…what if feels like to have some affection
from a relationship or a friend…

475
00:21:44,678 --> 00:21:46,972
- [Maririn] Yeah.
- …so, I think it's gonna be important

476
00:21:47,055 --> 00:21:48,849
- we share that with you.
- [Maririn] Totally.

477
00:21:48,932 --> 00:21:52,311
At the very least, none of the guys here
would ever treat you like that, right?

478
00:21:52,394 --> 00:21:54,229
- [Bo] Mmm-hmm.
- [Tai-chan] For sure.

479
00:21:54,313 --> 00:21:56,523
If you don't say it out loud,
nothing will change.

480
00:21:56,606 --> 00:21:57,733
- [Ruru] Yeah.
- [Ma-kun] True.

481
00:21:58,400 --> 00:22:01,153
I realize now it's not gonna help
to keep it all inside.

482
00:22:01,236 --> 00:22:03,238
- [Assun] Exactly.
- [Leo] Thank you.

483
00:22:03,322 --> 00:22:05,365
- [Maririn] Thanks.
- [Leo] You did good.

484
00:22:05,449 --> 00:22:07,451
- [Ari] That was incredible.
- Thank you.

485
00:22:07,534 --> 00:22:08,702
[both giggling]

486
00:22:09,369 --> 00:22:10,912
[Ruru] I love you, Maririn.

487
00:22:11,580 --> 00:22:12,831
- [chuckles]
- Love you too.

488
00:22:13,540 --> 00:22:15,542
[bell chiming]

489
00:22:19,546 --> 00:22:23,467
[boy on PA] <i>This part of Okinawa</i>
<i>is struggling with an aging population.</i>

490
00:22:23,550 --> 00:22:25,635
<i>It's becoming a serious problem.</i>

491
00:22:26,345 --> 00:22:31,516
<i>So, we ask you to use your youthful energy</i>
<i>to help the people around you.</i>

492
00:22:32,350 --> 00:22:36,688
<i>At one time, all of you</i>
<i>have had the experience of not fitting in,</i>

493
00:22:36,772 --> 00:22:38,982
<i>and now, through this experience,</i>

494
00:22:39,066 --> 00:22:44,613
<i>you will have a chance to learn about</i>
<i>community and find future inspiration.</i>

495
00:22:47,240 --> 00:22:49,284
This time around,
there are a lot of participants

496
00:22:49,367 --> 00:22:51,703
who have had
these rather heavy experiences.

497
00:22:51,787 --> 00:22:53,038
There are quite a lot of them.

498
00:22:53,121 --> 00:22:56,333
First, you had Bo, with his story
about his addiction to meth.

499
00:22:56,416 --> 00:22:58,585
- Thank God he was able to kick the habit.
- I know.

500
00:22:58,668 --> 00:23:00,796
I think it takes a lot of courage

501
00:23:00,879 --> 00:23:03,381
- to be willing to share that too.
- [Awich] I agree.

502
00:23:03,465 --> 00:23:05,967
I keep thinking of how Maririn
was so reserved at first.

503
00:23:06,051 --> 00:23:07,761
- [Megumi] Yeah.
- It's 'cause of trauma.

504
00:23:07,844 --> 00:23:09,429
- [Megumi] True.
- I was in a relationship

505
00:23:09,513 --> 00:23:12,349
where I was the victim
of domestic violence,

506
00:23:12,432 --> 00:23:14,518
- earlier in my life.
- [Megumi] Oh, I see.

507
00:23:14,601 --> 00:23:17,354
People that abuse their partners
usually have a long history of it,

508
00:23:17,437 --> 00:23:20,273
and that cycle of violence
is really hard to stop.

509
00:23:20,357 --> 00:23:23,693
All that changes is their victims.
So once I saw the pattern,

510
00:23:23,777 --> 00:23:27,447
I was able to work up the courage
to eventually break free from it.

511
00:23:27,531 --> 00:23:28,865
- Mmm.
- [Nagano] Wow.

512
00:23:28,949 --> 00:23:31,868
With Maririn, the fact that
she's participating in this…

513
00:23:31,952 --> 00:23:32,828
[Nagano] Mmm.

514
00:23:32,911 --> 00:23:35,205
…means she's trying
to take a step forward.

515
00:23:35,288 --> 00:23:36,164
[Nagano] Makes sense.

516
00:23:36,248 --> 00:23:39,417
It's also a good sign she's saying
that kind of thing in front of everyone.

517
00:23:39,501 --> 00:23:42,754
It could mean that she's trying
to put that story behind her,

518
00:23:42,838 --> 00:23:45,715
trying to look beyond her victimhood
and move toward a brighter future.

519
00:23:45,799 --> 00:23:46,925
[Nagano] That's great.

520
00:23:47,008 --> 00:23:49,010
[upbeat music playing]

521
00:23:49,803 --> 00:23:51,930
- [Assun] Wait for me, guys!
- [Ari] The air is cleaner.

522
00:23:52,013 --> 00:23:53,515
- [laughing]
- Hey, how are you!?

523
00:23:53,598 --> 00:23:55,600
- [Higa] Just dandy. Come on over.
- Good?

524
00:23:55,684 --> 00:23:57,185
- Hello. Take a look.
- Amazing!

525
00:23:57,269 --> 00:23:58,854
[Ma-kun] It's in the middle of nowhere.

526
00:23:58,937 --> 00:24:01,773
- I could use a walking stick.
- [Higa] Exactly, we're in the mountains.

527
00:24:01,857 --> 00:24:04,818
- [Ruru] Feels super refreshing
- [Hikaru] Nice to meet you.

528
00:24:04,901 --> 00:24:07,487
- [Assun] Nice to meet you.
- [Higa] You're all part of the group?

529
00:24:07,571 --> 00:24:08,780
- [Leo] We are.
- [Bo] Yes.

530
00:24:08,864 --> 00:24:10,031
[Higa] Here, take this.

531
00:24:11,950 --> 00:24:13,076
- Okay.
- [Ari] A letter?

532
00:24:13,660 --> 00:24:15,036
"Ms. Higa was…

533
00:24:15,120 --> 00:24:18,623
an interpreter for American doctors
after the Second World War."

534
00:24:18,707 --> 00:24:20,667
"For decades, she has worked diligently

535
00:24:20,750 --> 00:24:24,629
to save the lives of many local people
suffering from serious illnesses."

536
00:24:24,713 --> 00:24:27,966
"Ms. Higa is currently protecting
this vast nature preserve,

537
00:24:28,049 --> 00:24:31,052
where the original landscape of Okinawa
shines through."

538
00:24:31,553 --> 00:24:33,263
"Please use your youthful energy

539
00:24:33,346 --> 00:24:36,349
to help the locals who protect
the beautiful land of Okinawa

540
00:24:36,433 --> 00:24:38,727
and its plentiful natural resources."

541
00:24:38,810 --> 00:24:39,936
- Okay.
- [Ma-kun] Sounds good.

542
00:24:40,020 --> 00:24:42,480
- It's nice to meet you all.
- [Bo] We're all happy to be here.

543
00:24:42,564 --> 00:24:43,565
MS. HIGA

544
00:24:43,648 --> 00:24:46,651
Sometimes, we also take care
of local kids.

545
00:24:46,735 --> 00:24:49,362
- You know, children with disabilities.
- [Assun] Okay.

546
00:24:49,446 --> 00:24:51,573
Lots of those kids
don't have many friends.

547
00:24:51,656 --> 00:24:54,826
So I try to help them
by keeping them company,

548
00:24:54,910 --> 00:24:56,912
even if it's for an hour or two.

549
00:24:56,995 --> 00:24:59,164
I try to get them
to go for nice long walks

550
00:24:59,247 --> 00:25:00,790
or to do activities together.

551
00:25:00,874 --> 00:25:02,375
That way, they sleep better at night.

552
00:25:03,168 --> 00:25:04,753
The most important thing for me

553
00:25:04,836 --> 00:25:08,256
is that this place continues
to help underprivileged children.

554
00:25:08,340 --> 00:25:10,592
So, please, come back as much as you can.

555
00:25:10,675 --> 00:25:13,053
Okay? So are you all from the mainland?

556
00:25:13,136 --> 00:25:15,555
- Yes, we are.
- I see. Gotcha.

557
00:25:15,639 --> 00:25:16,723
Right, right. <i>Joto!</i>

558
00:25:16,806 --> 00:25:17,724
- Yes!
<i>- Joto!</i>

559
00:25:17,807 --> 00:25:19,684
[all laughing] <i>Joto!</i>

560
00:25:19,768 --> 00:25:22,520
In Okinawa, whenever something
good happens and the stars align,

561
00:25:22,604 --> 00:25:23,438
you say, <i>"Joto."</i>

562
00:25:23,521 --> 00:25:24,940
- Oh, yeah.
- [Ruru] Seriously?

563
00:25:25,023 --> 00:25:28,193
We also say <i>"joto"</i> when we want
to give a compliment or say thank you.

564
00:25:28,276 --> 00:25:30,362
- I'll start using it after today.
- Yeah, <i>"Joto!"</i>

565
00:25:30,445 --> 00:25:32,948
- [Hikaru] Let's use it like crazy.
- Anyway, thanks for coming.

566
00:25:33,031 --> 00:25:34,324
Thank you for having us.

567
00:25:34,407 --> 00:25:35,784
<i>- Joto!</i>
- [all laugh]

568
00:25:35,867 --> 00:25:38,578
- Yep, that's how we roll in Okinawa.
- [Nagano] That's a real word?

569
00:25:38,662 --> 00:25:41,456
We use that term for anything, like,
"Oh, that outfit is <i>joto. "</i>

570
00:25:41,539 --> 00:25:44,167
Oh! So she wasn't saying that
to make it part of the show?

571
00:25:44,251 --> 00:25:47,128
- I'd be surprised if she'd ever seen it.
- [all laughing]

572
00:25:47,212 --> 00:25:50,674
Okay, let's go pick
some shikuwasa, shall we?

573
00:25:50,757 --> 00:25:52,634
- [Ruru] Shikuwasa, really?
- Yes.

574
00:25:52,717 --> 00:25:54,219
- [Hikaru] Yay!
- There's a ton of them.

575
00:25:54,302 --> 00:25:56,388
- [Ruru] No way!
- There's no way we can pick them all.

576
00:25:56,471 --> 00:25:58,390
- So grab what you can…
- [Ma-kun] Great.

577
00:25:58,473 --> 00:26:00,725
…bring them back here,
and then squeeze them.

578
00:26:00,809 --> 00:26:02,477
So you can see the whole process,

579
00:26:02,560 --> 00:26:05,438
from when they're on the tree
up until they're bottled and ready.

580
00:26:05,522 --> 00:26:06,731
- Cool.
- [all] <i>Joto!</i>

581
00:26:06,815 --> 00:26:08,900
- [laughing]
<i>- Joto!</i>

582
00:26:08,984 --> 00:26:10,735
Okay! Yes, let's go, all right?

583
00:26:10,819 --> 00:26:12,570
- Let's go. Let's do this.
- Let's go.

584
00:26:12,654 --> 00:26:14,948
[indistinct chatter]

585
00:26:15,031 --> 00:26:16,700
- [Assun] Let's go.
- [Hikaru] They're huge!

586
00:26:16,783 --> 00:26:19,202
- [Higa] Here, there's a bunch.
- I feel like we'll pick a lot.

587
00:26:19,286 --> 00:26:21,746
- Oh, gosh, I hope you do.
- Isn't this great?

588
00:26:21,830 --> 00:26:23,873
- I wanna try the juice.
- Start here?

589
00:26:23,957 --> 00:26:26,042
[Higa] It's better for the tree
if you pick them all.

590
00:26:26,126 --> 00:26:27,877
- [Tai-chan] I didn't know that.
- That true?

591
00:26:27,961 --> 00:26:29,629
- [Tai-chan] Gotcha.
- [Ma-kun] Makes sense.

592
00:26:29,713 --> 00:26:30,547
- Let's do it.
- Okay.

593
00:26:30,630 --> 00:26:33,133
Man, I love this kind of thing. So dope.

594
00:26:33,216 --> 00:26:35,260
- [Maririn] How do you do it?
- Like this.

595
00:26:36,594 --> 00:26:38,763
- Have you done this kind of thing before?
- [Bo] No.

596
00:26:38,847 --> 00:26:41,057
- [laughs]
- [Higa] Don't be shy, get in there.

597
00:26:41,141 --> 00:26:42,183
Actually, in Juvie.

598
00:26:42,267 --> 00:26:44,019
- Juvie?
- [Nagano] <i>Said it like it's nothing.</i>

599
00:26:44,102 --> 00:26:45,729
- Put me on your shoulders.
- [Leo] Hop on.

600
00:26:46,354 --> 00:26:47,772
- On my shoulders?
- [Ruru] Here I go.

601
00:26:47,856 --> 00:26:49,190
- [Leo] Okay.
- [Megumi]<i> Wow.</i>

602
00:26:49,274 --> 00:26:50,900
- [Ruru] Hold on.
- [Leo] Ready?

603
00:26:50,984 --> 00:26:54,487
- One, two, three, up we go.
- [Ruru] Oh, this is great.

604
00:26:54,988 --> 00:26:57,699
Don't smack me with a branch.
I'll lose an eye.

605
00:26:57,782 --> 00:27:00,285
- [Ruru laughing]
- And I'll be like, <i>"Joto!"</i> Thanks a lot.

606
00:27:00,994 --> 00:27:02,746
Quit laughing and pick 'em already.

607
00:27:02,829 --> 00:27:04,539
Oh, my God, you're the worst, Leo.

608
00:27:04,622 --> 00:27:06,207
[Megumi]<i> They're getting a lot closer.</i>

609
00:27:06,291 --> 00:27:07,959
- There's a tiny one here.
- Check this one.

610
00:27:08,043 --> 00:27:09,210
Oh, that looks great.

611
00:27:11,171 --> 00:27:14,424
[Ruru] Doesn't it feel great
that we're helping out by doing this?

612
00:27:14,507 --> 00:27:15,508
[Ma-kun] For sure.

613
00:27:16,259 --> 00:27:19,971
I've, um, done a lot of different kinds
of volunteer work.

614
00:27:20,055 --> 00:27:21,973
It definitely feeds me.

615
00:27:22,057 --> 00:27:25,435
I'm the type of person who finds
a lot of meaning in serving others.

616
00:27:26,394 --> 00:27:28,646
Like, after the earthquake in 2011,

617
00:27:28,730 --> 00:27:31,524
I was around 15 at the time,
so I was pretty young,

618
00:27:31,608 --> 00:27:34,152
but I went to do volunteer work then too.

619
00:27:34,986 --> 00:27:37,822
Now, I help out at cafeterias
for children in need.

620
00:27:37,906 --> 00:27:39,574
I donate to places like that too.

621
00:27:39,657 --> 00:27:42,410
I like to spend my money on things
that can help people.

622
00:27:42,494 --> 00:27:44,204
- Impressive.
- Amazing. So cool.

623
00:27:44,287 --> 00:27:45,288
Well done.

624
00:27:46,331 --> 00:27:49,167
[Maririn] If you've been to prison,
can you legally get a passport?

625
00:27:49,250 --> 00:27:51,211
[Nagano]
<i>What the heck are they talking about?</i>

626
00:27:51,294 --> 00:27:54,047
[Bo] You might be able to get one
for the US and Central America,

627
00:27:54,130 --> 00:27:56,508
but there's some kind of long process.

628
00:27:56,591 --> 00:27:58,551
- [Maririn] Really?
- [Bo] I have a criminal record.

629
00:27:58,635 --> 00:28:01,054
- That's right.
- I can't travel there.

630
00:28:01,137 --> 00:28:03,848
If you have a criminal record,
it's a lot harder to get a passport.

631
00:28:03,932 --> 00:28:05,475
Oh, okay, so that's true.

632
00:28:05,558 --> 00:28:09,229
- You know everything, professor.
- [Nagano] She does! World traveler here.

633
00:28:09,312 --> 00:28:11,356
- [Tai-chan] Hey, Hikaru.
- [Hikaru] Hmm?

634
00:28:11,439 --> 00:28:14,150
- [Tai-chan] Let's start picking over here.
- [Hikaru] Sounds good.

635
00:28:15,193 --> 00:28:17,529
- [Ari] Look, it's huge!
- [Tai-chan] You use purple shampoo?

636
00:28:17,612 --> 00:28:19,739
- [Hikaru] Yeah.
- [Tai-chan] I knew it. I use it too.

637
00:28:19,823 --> 00:28:22,325
- [Awich]<i> Well, he's a hairstylist.</i>
- [Megumi]<i> That explains it.</i>

638
00:28:22,409 --> 00:28:23,576
[Tai-chan] You're cute.

639
00:28:25,036 --> 00:28:26,413
- Did you just blush?
- [Hikaru] Hmm?

640
00:28:26,496 --> 00:28:28,123
- Did you just blush?
- Nah.

641
00:28:28,206 --> 00:28:30,458
- You didn't blush?
- No, but that gave me a good boost.

642
00:28:30,542 --> 00:28:33,378
- [Tai-chan] Really? You're cute.
- [Hikaru] Yeah. [laughs]

643
00:28:33,461 --> 00:28:35,713
You're like a rebellious,
feminist white girl.

644
00:28:35,797 --> 00:28:37,298
[Hikaru] I'm not a white girl!

645
00:28:37,382 --> 00:28:39,551
- Your skin's pretty light.
- [Hikaru] My Korean side.

646
00:28:39,634 --> 00:28:40,885
Oh, you're Korean?

647
00:28:40,969 --> 00:28:42,929
- I have a Korean sense of style.
- [Hikaru] Do you?

648
00:28:43,012 --> 00:28:45,348
- We like the same fashion.
- Well, I'm a quarter Korean.

649
00:28:45,432 --> 00:28:47,308
- [Ari] What?
- [Hikaru] Yeah, I am.

650
00:28:47,392 --> 00:28:49,477
If you saw me without makeup,
you'd be able to tell.

651
00:28:49,561 --> 00:28:51,354
- Now I wanna see you without makeup.
- Okay.

652
00:28:51,438 --> 00:28:52,355
- For real?
- Sure.

653
00:28:53,398 --> 00:28:55,358
[Ari] That's all I can think about now.

654
00:28:55,984 --> 00:28:58,278
[Hikaru] Then keep daydreaming
while you pick shikuwasa.

655
00:28:58,361 --> 00:28:59,404
[Ari] Yes, ma'am.

656
00:29:00,196 --> 00:29:02,824
[Hikaru] Oh! Whoops, dropped one.
It almost landed on your head.

657
00:29:04,659 --> 00:29:06,244
I don't know. I was just like,

658
00:29:06,327 --> 00:29:08,705
"She's always talking to Taisei."
Like… [groans]

659
00:29:08,788 --> 00:29:11,124
And, if we're gonna go that route,
bring it on.

660
00:29:11,958 --> 00:29:15,336
If we end up liking the same person,
we'll just go head to head.

661
00:29:15,420 --> 00:29:19,090
So, yeah, if he wants to be rivals,
let's do it. That's where I'm at.

662
00:29:19,174 --> 00:29:20,759
She'll see I'm a better match.

663
00:29:20,842 --> 00:29:23,970
I wanna show her that her future
would be better with me in it.

664
00:29:24,053 --> 00:29:25,430
Better than with Taisei.

665
00:29:26,598 --> 00:29:29,184
- Gosh, it smells good.
- Yeah, get a whiff of that!

666
00:29:29,267 --> 00:29:31,603
- [Assun] I think they have to wash these.
- [Higa] Good job.

667
00:29:31,686 --> 00:29:33,104
- [Higa] This way.
- Yeah.

668
00:29:33,188 --> 00:29:35,148
- [Higa] We make the juice here.
- Thanks!

669
00:29:35,231 --> 00:29:36,232
[Higa] Yep.

670
00:29:36,733 --> 00:29:37,734
- [grunts]
- [Leo] Hmm?

671
00:29:37,817 --> 00:29:38,818
[Higa] Okay.

672
00:29:38,902 --> 00:29:41,696
- [Ruru] Must be tough doing this.
- [Hikaru] Let me see.

673
00:29:41,780 --> 00:29:45,074
- [Bo] Careful, water's hot.
- We don't normally do stuff like this.

674
00:29:45,784 --> 00:29:47,368
- Great experience.
- [Bo] Towel, please.

675
00:29:48,411 --> 00:29:51,456
- [Higa] That tattoo, is that a map?
- I get asked that a lot.

676
00:29:51,539 --> 00:29:54,000
- [laughing] Love that. She's so curious.
- [Megumi] Oh, wow.

677
00:29:54,083 --> 00:29:55,210
Yep. She's fearless.

678
00:29:55,293 --> 00:29:57,337
- It looks like a map.
- [Tai-chan] It's not a map.

679
00:29:57,420 --> 00:29:58,505
- It's not?
- It's lightning.

680
00:29:58,588 --> 00:29:59,881
- Lightning?
- Uh, yeah.

681
00:29:59,964 --> 00:30:02,300
I'm surprised you'd draw lightning
on such a pretty face.

682
00:30:02,383 --> 00:30:05,011
- You think it's pretty?
- [Higa] Of course, you're handsome!

683
00:30:05,094 --> 00:30:07,138
[Tai-chan] That's flattering. Thank you.

684
00:30:08,807 --> 00:30:10,433
- [Higa] See that?
- [Leo] Mmm-hmm.

685
00:30:10,517 --> 00:30:12,685
- [Ruru] Amazing!
- [Higa] Pretty cool, right?

686
00:30:12,769 --> 00:30:15,313
- [Leo] Oh, yeah!
- [Ruru] That's seriously amazing.

687
00:30:15,396 --> 00:30:17,440
[Bo] So, do they add sugar at all?

688
00:30:17,524 --> 00:30:19,776
- [Assun] 'Course you'd ask that.
- [Bo laughs]

689
00:30:24,030 --> 00:30:26,866
- [Ma-kun] It smells so good.
- [Higa] Okay, gather around.

690
00:30:26,950 --> 00:30:28,701
- Let's eat first.
- [Ruru] Yeah, I'm hungry.

691
00:30:28,785 --> 00:30:30,787
- [Tai-chan] Looks incredible.
- [Higa] Here you go.

692
00:30:30,870 --> 00:30:33,164
- [Ruru] Looks so good.
- [Tai-chan] Can't wait.

693
00:30:33,706 --> 00:30:35,500
- Okay, dig in.
- Thanks for all this.

694
00:30:35,583 --> 00:30:37,126
- Looks incredible.
- Thank you.

695
00:30:37,210 --> 00:30:39,921
- [Hikaru] I want the juice first.
- [Higa] Does everyone have a cup?

696
00:30:40,004 --> 00:30:41,089
- Is it good?
- Sour!

697
00:30:41,172 --> 00:30:42,799
- [Tai-chan] Yum.
- [Higa] Tart, right?

698
00:30:42,882 --> 00:30:45,677
- [Megumi]<i> I bet that stuff's good for you.</i>
- It's tasty.

699
00:30:45,760 --> 00:30:46,719
[Higa] You like it?

700
00:30:46,803 --> 00:30:48,179
- [Ruru] Delicious!
- Food's amazing.

701
00:30:48,263 --> 00:30:49,347
- [Higa] Good?
- Yeah.

702
00:30:49,430 --> 00:30:51,432
[Higa] That's good to hear. But, listen.

703
00:30:52,016 --> 00:30:54,519
No matter what happened in your past,

704
00:30:54,602 --> 00:30:58,314
if you're happy right now
and you have a decent job,

705
00:30:58,398 --> 00:31:00,441
isn't that really all you need in life?

706
00:31:00,525 --> 00:31:03,194
Because, you know,
in this day and age, well,

707
00:31:03,278 --> 00:31:06,447
things are… things are getting
a little dark and scary.

708
00:31:06,531 --> 00:31:10,034
Children killing their parents,
and parents killing their children,

709
00:31:10,118 --> 00:31:12,579
it's really painful
just to think about it.

710
00:31:12,662 --> 00:31:16,082
When I hear about these terrible things,
it makes me wonder how…

711
00:31:16,165 --> 00:31:19,961
I mean, they probably felt like they had
a good reason to do it at the time,

712
00:31:20,587 --> 00:31:22,422
but I always wonder if there was anything

713
00:31:22,505 --> 00:31:26,092
that could've been done
to prevent it from happening. Hmm?

714
00:31:26,175 --> 00:31:28,595
So, I think it's a good idea
for all of you

715
00:31:28,678 --> 00:31:30,597
to keep that in mind in the future.

716
00:31:31,890 --> 00:31:34,976
Uh, I think a lot of us here,
we wanna find love.

717
00:31:35,059 --> 00:31:35,935
[Higa] Mmm-hmm.

718
00:31:36,019 --> 00:31:38,605
What should we do
if we find someone we're interested in?

719
00:31:38,688 --> 00:31:42,233
That's easy.
Put on a nice, big smile and say hello!

720
00:31:42,317 --> 00:31:44,193
- [Ruru laughs] So cute!
- That works.

721
00:31:44,277 --> 00:31:47,614
- [Assun] Might be the best first step.
- I'm not kidding. That's what I'd do.

722
00:31:47,697 --> 00:31:50,450
- If you find someone you like.
- Should we just say how we feel?

723
00:31:50,533 --> 00:31:52,410
Don't confess right away.

724
00:31:52,493 --> 00:31:55,204
- Little by little?
- [Higa] Don't scare them off.

725
00:31:55,788 --> 00:31:58,207
Even if you want to tell them right away,

726
00:31:58,291 --> 00:32:00,335
if you just tell her everything at once,

727
00:32:00,418 --> 00:32:03,129
she might get overwhelmed with anxiety
and pull away.

728
00:32:03,212 --> 00:32:04,213
- [Ari] Mmm.
- Mmm.

729
00:32:04,297 --> 00:32:06,841
- That's great advice from a legend.
- A legend, huh?

730
00:32:06,925 --> 00:32:09,636
- Totally. Hit the nail on the head.
- She's got all the dating tips.

731
00:32:09,719 --> 00:32:10,678
That makes sense.

732
00:32:10,762 --> 00:32:12,639
- [Higa] Best of luck.
- Thanks, I'll need it.

733
00:32:12,722 --> 00:32:14,641
- [Ruru] She's too much.
- [Ari] Aye-aye, captain!

734
00:32:15,850 --> 00:32:18,978
- We had an amazing time.
- [Higa] Really? I'm glad to hear that.

735
00:32:19,062 --> 00:32:21,022
We'd never get an experience like this.

736
00:32:21,105 --> 00:32:23,066
What time we meeting tomorrow?
To chop wood?

737
00:32:23,149 --> 00:32:25,068
[all laugh]

738
00:32:25,151 --> 00:32:27,278
- [Leo] Noon?
- Let's see. What time is good?

739
00:32:27,362 --> 00:32:29,197
- 5:00 a.m. sharp?
- [all laughing]

740
00:32:29,280 --> 00:32:30,865
Sorry, uh, no, no, sorry.

741
00:32:30,949 --> 00:32:32,533
- I was kidding.
- [Higa] Kidding?

742
00:32:32,617 --> 00:32:34,327
- I got carried away.
- [Higa] Right.

743
00:32:37,497 --> 00:32:40,166
Uh, so, did anybody else
notice that old lady's hands?

744
00:32:40,833 --> 00:32:42,126
- They were brown.
- [Hikaru] Yeah.

745
00:32:42,210 --> 00:32:45,213
I think that comes from
going through that process every day.

746
00:32:45,296 --> 00:32:47,548
Her hands tell the story
of the work she does.

747
00:32:48,341 --> 00:32:50,718
- It's gotta be tough.
- [Ma-kun] Dude. For sure.

748
00:32:50,802 --> 00:32:53,554
When you stop and think
she's been doing that every day

749
00:32:53,638 --> 00:32:56,307
for the past 40 years,
it's seriously amazing, right?

750
00:32:56,391 --> 00:32:58,393
- She's so cool.
- That kind of environment

751
00:32:58,476 --> 00:33:01,771
can really be good for troubled kids.
It's perfect for them.

752
00:33:01,854 --> 00:33:04,148
They get that level of care and attention.

753
00:33:05,274 --> 00:33:08,486
And then, the kids who got
that kind of help in life,

754
00:33:08,569 --> 00:33:11,823
they eventually grow up,
and they have the tools and opportunities

755
00:33:11,906 --> 00:33:14,867
to give back to kids
in the same situation they were in.

756
00:33:14,951 --> 00:33:17,453
- I just think that's really wonderful.
- Mmm.

757
00:33:18,413 --> 00:33:19,664
Yeah, I really think…

758
00:33:20,289 --> 00:33:23,251
we'd all be better off
if we tried to value stuff like that.

759
00:33:23,334 --> 00:33:25,878
- Definitely.
- That old lady was so warm and sweet.

760
00:33:25,962 --> 00:33:26,963
[bell chiming]

761
00:33:27,046 --> 00:33:30,383
[Megumi] <i>I'm glad everyone had a chance</i>
<i>to take in that experience.</i>

762
00:33:32,343 --> 00:33:34,303
[boy on PA]
<i>Time for the evening sauna session.</i>

763
00:33:34,387 --> 00:33:35,430
- [Ruru] Oh?
- Oh, now?

764
00:33:35,513 --> 00:33:38,057
[boy on PA] <i>The person selected</i>
<i>for the sauna this time</i>

765
00:33:38,141 --> 00:33:42,270
<i>was able to find their courage,</i>
<i>and open up about their past.</i>

766
00:33:43,229 --> 00:33:44,605
<i>- Congrats, Maririn.</i>
- [Hikaru] What?

767
00:33:44,689 --> 00:33:45,690
[Ari] Maririn, yeah!

768
00:33:45,773 --> 00:33:48,151
[boy on PA] <i>You may now choose the man</i>
<i>you're interested in.</i>

769
00:33:48,234 --> 00:33:50,862
- [Ari] Well deserved!
- [Ruru] This is so exciting.

770
00:33:50,945 --> 00:33:53,072
- [Leo] She was so brave!
- [Ari] So happy for you.

771
00:33:53,156 --> 00:33:55,575
- [Ruru] You killed it.
- [Maririn] For real. Okay.

772
00:33:55,658 --> 00:33:57,326
Let me see… Wait, this feels like

773
00:33:57,410 --> 00:33:59,746
- a really tough decision.
- [Hikaru] This is tricky.

774
00:33:59,829 --> 00:34:02,040
How about we have the guys
go somewhere else?

775
00:34:02,123 --> 00:34:03,750
- [Ari] Good idea.
- For a little bit.

776
00:34:03,833 --> 00:34:06,044
- The guys will go somewhere.
- We'll call you back.

777
00:34:06,127 --> 00:34:08,296
- [Leo] Don't want us eavesdropping.
- [Hikaru] Exactly.

778
00:34:08,379 --> 00:34:10,423
- [Ari] No problem.
- Wanna talk about it?

779
00:34:10,506 --> 00:34:12,133
- [Maririn] I guess so.
- Sit here.

780
00:34:12,216 --> 00:34:13,468
So, how many are there?

781
00:34:13,551 --> 00:34:14,802
- [Maririn] What?
- Choices?

782
00:34:14,886 --> 00:34:17,013
- Let's see…
- [Ari] Boys, hit the road.

783
00:34:17,764 --> 00:34:21,976
Okay, so, like, I've been talking
to Tai-chan, but, well…

784
00:34:22,935 --> 00:34:25,396
- [giggling]
- [chuckling]

785
00:34:25,480 --> 00:34:27,106
But, honestly, I'm thinking Leo.

786
00:34:27,190 --> 00:34:28,608
- Oh!
- Yeah, so…

787
00:34:29,525 --> 00:34:33,154
'Cause, I don't know, I don't think
Tai-chan wants to keep talking to me.

788
00:34:33,237 --> 00:34:36,491
I gave him a letter yesterday,
but he hasn't said anything since.

789
00:34:36,574 --> 00:34:38,951
[Megumi] <i>Interesting.</i>
<i>So she's sensing something is off.</i>

790
00:34:39,035 --> 00:34:40,369
[Ruru] So Tai-chan or Leo?

791
00:34:40,453 --> 00:34:41,579
- I think so.
- [Ruru] For now.

792
00:34:42,663 --> 00:34:45,208
To be honest,
I wanna cook with Leo after this.

793
00:34:45,291 --> 00:34:47,877
- So I don't want him to go.
- [Assun] Oh!

794
00:34:47,960 --> 00:34:49,879
- It's heating up in here.
- [Nagano] <i>Shots fired.</i>

795
00:34:49,962 --> 00:34:52,715
[Ruru] You decided?
What should we do with the guys?

796
00:34:52,799 --> 00:34:55,426
- Guys, we're ready.
- [Megumi]<i> They really did stay away, huh?</i>

797
00:34:55,510 --> 00:34:57,512
- [Awich]<i> They're running back.</i>
- [Megumi]<i> So cute.</i>

798
00:34:58,471 --> 00:34:59,889
[Ari] Wassup, wassup?

799
00:34:59,972 --> 00:35:02,975
- God, they're all just staring her down.
- They're all looking at me.

800
00:35:03,059 --> 00:35:04,644
- [laughs]
- Super intense.

801
00:35:04,727 --> 00:35:07,772
[Ruru] Maririn is about to say
who she wants to go into the sauna with.

802
00:35:08,439 --> 00:35:11,317
- [Ruru and Ari mimic drum roll]
- [laughs]

803
00:35:12,735 --> 00:35:14,028
- Leo.
- [Ma-kun exclaims]

804
00:35:14,612 --> 00:35:16,197
Okay, let's go.

805
00:35:16,280 --> 00:35:17,615
- [Hikaru] Nice.
- [Ruru] So fast.

806
00:35:17,698 --> 00:35:20,159
[Hikaru] You ever seen someone
jump up so fast?

807
00:35:20,243 --> 00:35:22,745
- [Assun] Everyone jumps at the chance.
- [Hikaru] Eager beaver.

808
00:35:22,829 --> 00:35:24,914
- [Nagano]<i> Wow!</i>
- Not fun for her, huh?

809
00:35:24,997 --> 00:35:27,250
- [chuckling] Not much of a poker face.
- [Megumi laughs]

810
00:35:27,333 --> 00:35:30,336
- She wears her heart on her sleeve.
- [Nagano] Girl can't hide her feelings.

811
00:35:30,419 --> 00:35:31,921
She puts everything out in the open.

812
00:35:33,339 --> 00:35:34,799
- [Maririn] Later.
- [Hikaru] Have fun.

813
00:35:41,305 --> 00:35:44,559
- [Assun] How are you feeling?
- Doesn't exactly make me feel great.

814
00:35:44,642 --> 00:35:45,893
- [Assun] Yeah, I bet.
- Mmm-hmm.

815
00:35:45,977 --> 00:35:48,396
I even told her
I didn't want her to go with Leo.

816
00:35:48,479 --> 00:35:50,690
- [Assun] I know.
- You told her? Just now?

817
00:35:50,773 --> 00:35:52,024
- [Ruru] I did.
- [Assun] She did.

818
00:35:52,108 --> 00:35:54,527
- [Ari] What did she say?
- [Ruru] She's going with him anyway.

819
00:35:54,610 --> 00:35:55,862
- She's feisty.
- [laughs]

820
00:35:55,945 --> 00:35:58,823
- Yeah. Maririn's a spicy one.
- [Ma-kun] Bro, she's built different.

821
00:36:00,241 --> 00:36:02,201
The thing is, I've never talked to him.

822
00:36:02,827 --> 00:36:05,204
And he's the one
I want to get to know the most.

823
00:36:05,288 --> 00:36:08,875
So, I'm really curious to see
what it's like with just the two of us.

824
00:36:08,958 --> 00:36:12,879
Maririn is basically…
She's only just beginning to open up.

825
00:36:12,962 --> 00:36:15,548
And it seems like
she wants to get to know everyone.

826
00:36:15,631 --> 00:36:18,384
And, don't get me wrong,
I want her to have a great time

827
00:36:18,467 --> 00:36:20,303
and fall in love with someone here.

828
00:36:20,887 --> 00:36:23,556
But if Maririn wants to go for Leo,
I'm cool with it,

829
00:36:23,639 --> 00:36:25,933
but I'm gonna be like,
"We're gonna throw down, girl."

830
00:36:26,017 --> 00:36:27,268
[Nagano]<i> Oh, that's good.</i>

831
00:36:27,351 --> 00:36:30,062
- That bathrobe looks good on you.
- You like it?

832
00:36:30,146 --> 00:36:31,939
[chuckles] You were made for that.

833
00:36:32,023 --> 00:36:33,983
- Feel like a rich guy.
- It's giving yakuza vibes.

834
00:36:34,066 --> 00:36:35,776
- Oh, come on.
- [Maririn giggling]

835
00:36:35,860 --> 00:36:36,861
Oh, wow.

836
00:36:37,695 --> 00:36:39,906
- [Maririn] Oh, you have tattoos.
- Yeah, I do.

837
00:36:39,989 --> 00:36:42,658
- For real? That's surprising.
- [Leo] Really? You think so?

838
00:36:42,742 --> 00:36:45,870
[Maririn] I didn't think you had any.
I saw the ones on your legs.

839
00:36:45,953 --> 00:36:48,122
- [Leo] Let's go in.
- [Maririn] Sounds good. [chuckles]

840
00:36:48,206 --> 00:36:50,541
[sultry music playing]

841
00:36:50,625 --> 00:36:53,294
- [Leo] Sandals. We can go with these.
- [Maririn] Let's put them on.

842
00:36:53,377 --> 00:36:55,296
- [Leo] Ready?
- [Maririn] Yeah. Oh, it's hot.

843
00:36:55,379 --> 00:36:56,797
[Leo] Why did you choose me?

844
00:36:56,881 --> 00:37:00,384
[Maririn] I thought the way
you listened to her was was really nice.

845
00:37:00,468 --> 00:37:02,637
Yeah. Oh, I've got a bunch
of back tats too.

846
00:37:02,720 --> 00:37:04,180
Wow, that's incredible.

847
00:37:04,263 --> 00:37:06,724
- [Maririn] How far do these go?
- [Leo] Nice, yeah? Butt crack.

848
00:37:06,807 --> 00:37:08,893
- No kidding. It's really--
- Like 'em?

849
00:37:08,976 --> 00:37:11,520
[Maririn] They look amazing.
I don't know much about art, but--

850
00:37:11,604 --> 00:37:14,106
- [Leo] The colors are pretty bold, right?
- [Maririn] So wild.

851
00:37:14,190 --> 00:37:15,816
It caught me off guard, and I love it.

852
00:37:15,900 --> 00:37:18,319
- [Leo] You didn't expect it? It's a plus.
- Yeah, not at all.

853
00:37:18,402 --> 00:37:19,403
- Yeah.
- [Leo] That's good.

854
00:37:19,487 --> 00:37:21,572
Everything the girls say about you
is a plus too.

855
00:37:21,656 --> 00:37:23,616
- [Maririn chuckles]
- Uh… Mmm.

856
00:37:23,699 --> 00:37:25,326
You seem like a really nice guy.

857
00:37:25,409 --> 00:37:29,121
I loved the way you were listening earlier
to, um, Higa, that old lady?

858
00:37:29,205 --> 00:37:31,290
- You were looking her in the eye.
- Mmm.

859
00:37:31,874 --> 00:37:33,209
That's when I started thinking,

860
00:37:33,292 --> 00:37:34,794
- "Maybe he's a good guy."
- Mmm.

861
00:37:37,004 --> 00:37:40,716
[boy on PA] <i>All of you worked hard</i>
<i>to help someone from the community,</i>

862
00:37:40,800 --> 00:37:43,970
<i>so as a reward for your commitment,</i>
<i>you may have alcohol.</i>

863
00:37:44,053 --> 00:37:46,013
- Yay!
- [Megumi]<i> Look how happy Assun is.</i>

864
00:37:46,097 --> 00:37:48,516
- <i>I love it.</i>
- [Ruru] Let's make dinner!

865
00:37:48,599 --> 00:37:50,851
- [Ma-kun] Heck yeah!
- [Ruru] This is the best.

866
00:37:50,935 --> 00:37:52,853
[Ma-kun] Maybe I'll become
a shikuwasa farmer.

867
